<title>USA: FirstFed raises credit card loss provision.</title>
<headline>FirstFed raises credit card loss provision.</headline>
<dateline>DES PLAINES, Ill. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>FirstFed Bancshares Inc said it raised its provision for credit card loan losses to $375,000 in the fourth quarter from $150,000 in the year ago quarter.</p>
<p>The company and the banking industry as a whole are beginning to see more credit card charge-offs resulting from personal bankruptcies, FirstFed said.</p>
<p>Earlier, FirstFed reported net income of $605,000, or $0.17 a share for the fourth quarter, compared to $450,000, or $0.12 a share a year ago.</p>
<p>FirstFed shares were unchanged at 16-3/4 Thursday.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
